invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_mul.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: window 0 adds its entry by the incomplete Jacobian addition in
  place of the complete one. For k = n - 2 and n - 3 the sum before
  window 0 is -p, and so is the entry, so the addition gives Z3 = 0: k * p
  comes out as the point at infinity for n - 2, and as -p for n - 3, whose
  correction then takes p away. Every other scalar is still right.
  bin/p256_equiv_test multiplies a point by both.

--- old
    p256_wide_point_from_jacobian(&total, &sum);
    p256_wide_point_from_jacobian(&last, &entry);
    p256_wide_point_add(&total, &total, &last);
--- new
    p256_wide_point_add_jacobian_incomplete(&sum, &sum, &entry);
    p256_wide_point_from_jacobian(&total, &sum);
